From 6f54d7ec8f42839ec6701c30b0d37873b5d6620d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baptiste Pignier <pignier.baptiste@tutanota.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:41:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] goodixtls53xd: Make captures usable on 27c6:538d

- Average the frames of a press instead of assembling them like a swipe:
  the 53xd is a press sensor and every frame covers the same area.
- Capture a background frame without finger before each scan and subtract
  it from the press (the previous subtraction code was disabled and wrong).
- Remove each row mean, crop a 2 pixel border and stretch between the 2nd
  and 98th percentiles: removes horizontal bands and border outliers.
- Write 05 03 to sensor register 0x022c as the Python driver does, the
  guint16 brace initializer sent 05 00.
- Detect the finger by polling frames against the background instead of
  FDT down: the FDT thresholds are hardcoded from another sensor and fired
  without finger. Wait for the finger to be lifted before reporting it.
- Use the OTP calibration bytes in the FDT mode command too.
- Complete the scan state machine before reporting finger off, so the next
  scan isn't lost (double free on close), and stop polling on deactivate.
- Optionally dump the produced image to $GOODIX53XD_DUMP_DIR for debugging.

Capture, enroll and finger detection work. NBIS finds only 1 or 2 minutiae
per 60x76 image, so verification doesn't match.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
